        "collisionAnalysis": "In legacy storage, identity is composite key (ls_img_name, ls_img_sha1, ls_name, ls_page), so both sets use ls_name='default' without collision. In page-owned documents, surface 'id' must be globally unique across the document, but 'label' does not need to be unique. The converter must NOT map ls_name directly to surface id; it must assign distinct stable surface IDs (e.g. 'surface_q1_rev' and 'surface_q2_rev') while preserving the shared display label 'Figure 1: Revenue'.",
